+  // Korri runtime-bitrate experiment: FFmpeg's VAAPI encoder keeps the
+  // VAEncMiscParameterRateControl struct in private VAAPIEncodeContext state
+  // and stores a pointer to it in the per-IDR global-params list. Mutating that
+  // struct on the encode thread, then forcing an IDR, lets FFmpeg re-upload the
+  // updated rate-control buffer without recreating the VA context.
+  //
+  // This mirrors FFmpeg 8 / libavcodec 62.11.100 private structs through the
+  // fields we mutate. It is intentionally constrained to h264_vaapi and guarded
+  // by runtime sanity checks because this is not a public FFmpeg ABI.
